  console.log('Key is removed');
});
```

In this example, the `chrome.storage.local` object is used to access `localStorage`, which is shared between all pages of the same origin. You can also use the `chrome.storage.sync` object to synchronize data across devices.

Keep in mind that the `chrome.storage` API operates asynchronously, so you'll need to use a callback function to handle the result of each operation.

